//! Visual-Inertial Bundle Adjustment via dense Schur-complement reduction.
//!
//! Extends [`crate::schur_ba`] from 6-DOF visual BA to 15-DOF VI-BA by
//! adding IMU preintegration residuals between consecutive keyframes.
//!
//! ## State layout per keyframe
//!
//! ```text
//! x_i = [ ρ(3) | ω(3) | v(3) | b_g(3) | b_a(3) ]   (15-DOF tangent)
//!          pose(6)     vel(3)   gyro-bias  accel-bias
//! ```
//!
//! ## Block structure of the normal equations H·δx = b
//!
//! ```text
//!     H = [ A    E  ]     A  = 15P × 15P  (BLOCK-TRIDIAGONAL, not diagonal!)
//!         [ Eᵀ   C  ]     C  =  3N ×  3N  (block-diagonal, same as visual BA)
//!                          E  = 15P ×  3N  (sparse, visual obs only)
//! ```
//!
//! The tridiagonal structure of A comes from IMU residuals coupling frame i
//! and frame i+1 through off-diagonal 15×15 blocks. Visual residuals add
//! only to the diagonal 15×15 block of whichever frame they belong to.
//!
//! ## IMU residual (Mur-Artal & Tardós RA-L 2017, eq. 3-5)
//!
//! ```text
//! r_ΔR  = Log( ΔR̃ᵀ · Rᵢᵀ · Rⱼ )       ∈ ℝ³
//! r_Δv  = Rᵢᵀ(vⱼ - vᵢ - g·Δt) - Δṽ    ∈ ℝ³
//! r_Δp  = Rᵢᵀ(pⱼ - pᵢ - vᵢ·Δt - ½g·Δt²) - Δp̃  ∈ ℝ³
//! ```
//!
//! Jacobians use the preintegrated bias-correction Jacobians accumulated
//! inside [`PreintegratedImu`] during integration, so no re-integration
//! is needed when biases change within the BA loop.
//!
//! ## Schur elimination
//!
//! Identical to the pure-visual case — C (point block) is still block-diagonal
//! and cheap to invert. The reduced camera system S = A - E·C⁻¹·Eᵀ is now
//! 15P×15P (vs 6P×6P) but otherwise the same dense Cholesky solve applies.
//!
//! ## Reference
//! Mur-Artal, R. and Tardós, J.D. (2017). "Visual-Inertial Monocular SLAM
//! with Map Reuse." RA-L 2(2):796-803.

